3. TTL management → Avoid having a large number of popular keys expire at exactly the same time.

Imagine you have 1 million cache keys, and all of them have:

TTL = 1 hour

If they were all inserted around the same time:

10:00 AM → 1 million keys inserted
11:00 AM → 1 million keys expire
             ↓
      Cache becomes empty
             ↓
1 million requests → Cache MISS
             ↓
        Database
             ↓
      DB gets overloaded

This is called a cache stampede or thundering herd problem.


